{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2017-246", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/246", "wordCount": 1300, "segments": [{"start": 19.0, "text": "Hello and welcome to Deep"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "Linking on tvOS."}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "Today we will be looking at best"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "practices for supporting deep"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "links in your tvOS app."}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "So what is a deep link?"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "A deep link is a URL that your"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "application knows how to open."}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "We call these links in deep"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "because they often refer to"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "content that's a few levels down"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "in your App2i."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "Instead of manually navigating"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "through several screens, a user"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "can jump immediately to the"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "content they want by using the"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "deep link."}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "Deep link URLs can be sent to"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "your app from various parts of"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "the system or even other"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "One common source of deep links"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "is your application's top shelf"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "extension."}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "If you have a top shelf"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "extension, it communicates with"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "your app using deep links."}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "The code handles"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "links from the top shelf can"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "also be used to handle links"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "from any other source."}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "If you're not familiar with a top shelf, here's an example of"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "the top shelf extension for the"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "iTunes movie sound."}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "Each item in the top shelf will"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "open a different movie in the"}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "iTunes movie app."}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "Because these links are meant"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "for your application, we"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "recommend that you use universal"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "links."}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "Universal links can also be used"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "in your iOS app, if you have"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "one."}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "Unlike rolling your own custom"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "URL scheme, universal links"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "ensure that the link is always"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "routed to your application."}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "And that the data is in a format"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "your application expects."}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "For more information about"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "universal links, see the web"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "page at this URL."}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "So, now that you know what a"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "deep link is and where they come"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "from, let's take a look at what"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "you should do when your"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "application is asked to open"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "one."}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "The most important part is to"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "take the user to the link"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "content immediately, without any"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "loading screens or animated"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "transitions."}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "You should avoid any alerts"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "asking if the user is sure that"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "they want to open the link or"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "sure that they want to start"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "playing the video."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "It's also important to make sure"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "that when the user leaves link"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "content, they're able to orient"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "themselves in your app."}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "Even when jumping somewhere"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "directly, the user should always"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "know where they are and how they"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "got there."}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "How should you display deep link"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "content?"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "Well, it depends on the link."}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "Let's take a look at the top"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "shelf items again."}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "Each top shelf item supports two"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "URLs, the displayURL and the"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "playURL."}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "The displayURL is opened when"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "the user presses a select"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "button, and this should take the"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "user to a detail page for the"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "top shelf item."}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "And typically this detail page"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "will include a way to play the"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "item, if the item is a video."}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "The playURL is opened when the"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "user presses the Play button."}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "This is a shortcut that lets the"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "user immediately start video"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "playback for the item."}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "Remember, the displayURL should"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "take the user to a detail page"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "for the item."}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "Menuing out of this detail page"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "should take the user back to"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "your application's main screen."}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "Now it could be that the user"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "would normally have to navigate"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "through several levels to get to"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "the detail page from the main"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "screen, but they shouldn't have"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "to take multiple steps to back"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "out of a deep link."}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "Instead, the first Menu press"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "should take them back to the top"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "level of your application."}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "Because it's the top level, a"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "second Menu press should exit"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "the app and return to the tvOS"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "home screen."}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "And here's an illustration of"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "what that looks like."}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "Here, I've opened a deep link in"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "a simple video app."}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "The first screen I'm taken to is"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "a detail page for the video I've"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "selected."}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "Pressing Menu once takes me back"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "to my app's main screen, which"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "shows a grid of all the videos"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "that I can watch."}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "Pressing Menu again will exit my"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "app and take me back to the tvOS"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "home screen."}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "Now let's look at how to handle"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "a playURL."}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "Remember, this should"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "immediately begin video playback"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "for the item."}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "Your app should start with a"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "black screen and then fade in"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "the video."}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "Try to avoid any visible"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "transitions or user interaction"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "and this is especially important"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "for resuming playback of a video"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "that the user's already started"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "watching."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "Pressing Menu to exit playback"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "should take the user to the same"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "detail page you would have shown"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "if the displayURL had been sent."}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "From there, the navigation is"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "the same as before."}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "Menuing out of the detail page,"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "it should go to your apps main"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "screen and a second Menu press"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "should return to the tvOS home"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "screen."}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "And here's an illustration of"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "what that looks like."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "You can see that the first screen is a video playback and"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "then behind that, it's the same"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "hierarchy as if we had opened"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "the displayURL."}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "Now let's take a quick look at a"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "demo to really see these"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "concepts in action."}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "Here's a simple app that lets me"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "play some of my favorite videos"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "from WWDC. I can get to the videos from"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "within the app, but there's also"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "a top shelf extension that lets"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "me jump to the videos directly"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "from the tvOS home screen."}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "If I press select on a top shelf"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "item, I'm taken directly to the"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "detail page for that video."}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "If I go back to the top shelf --"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "And press play on a different"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "item, the app starts playing"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "that video."}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "Menuing out of playback takes me"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "to the detail page for the item"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "I was just watching."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "You'll remember that this isn't"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "the same item I was looking at"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "when I was last in the app and"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "that's because when the app"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "opened the link from the top"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "shelf, it reconfigured its UI to"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "display the link content."}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "Menu again takes me out of the"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "detail page and into the app's"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "main screen."}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "Pressing Menu a third time exits"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "the app and takes me back to the"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "tvOS home screen."}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "Let's take a quick look at the"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "code that handles deep linking"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "in this app."}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "The work happens in the app"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "delegate, specifically, the"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "application open url with"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "options method."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "First, when we reconfigure our"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "UI to display a deep link, we"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "want to do so without animation."}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "This means that the content will"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "already be displayed when the"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "system switches to our application."}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "Next, we want to tear down any"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "UI that the user may have"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "navigated to in a previous"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "session with the app."}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "This app is built using a navigation controller, so all we"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "have to do is pop back to the"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "root view controller, which is"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "the app's main screen."}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "And now, we want to push a"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "detail controller for the URL"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "onto the nav stack."}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "We want to do this even if we're"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "ultimately handling the playURL,"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "and that way the detail"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "controller will be there if the"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "user menu's out of playback."}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "And we'll push the detail"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "controller by performing the"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "same segue that would be"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "triggered if the user selected"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "one of the collection view cells"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "on the app's main screen."}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "Finally, if we're handling the"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "playURL, we want to push a"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "player view controller on top of"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "the detail view controller."}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "And we'll do this, again by"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "performing the same segue that"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "would be triggered if the user"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "had selected the Play button on"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "the detail screen."}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "In summary, deep links provide a"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "great way for users to quickly"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "navigate to content that may be"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "deep within your app."}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "When opening a deep link you'll"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "provide the best experience by"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "taking the user to the linked"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "content immediately and"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "providing them with a predictable way to get back."}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "For more information, please"}]}
